This solution uses vanilla JavaScript and CSS within a web component structure to achieve the desired functionality and styling.

### `x-details.js`

```javascript
class XDetails extends HTMLElement {
    constructor() {
        super();
        // Attach Shadow DOM
        this.attachShadow({ mode: 'open' });

        // Internal state
        this.isExpanded = false;

        // Render the initial structure
        this.render();

        // Set up event listeners for the toggle button
        this.shadowRoot.querySelector('.toggle-btn').addEventListener('click', this.toggle.bind(this));
    }

    // Renders the structural HTML inside the Shadow DOM
    render() {
        this.shadowRoot.innerHTML = `
            <style>
                :host {
                    display: block;
                    border: 1px solid #ccc;
                    border-radius: 4px;
                    margin-bottom: 10px;
                    font-family: sans-serif;
                }
                .details-container {
                    padding: 0 15px;
                }

                /* Header Style */
                .header {
                    display: flex;
                    align-items: center;
                    padding: 12px 0;
                    font-size: 1.1em;
                    font-weight: bold;
                    border-bottom: 1px solid #eee;
                    cursor: pointer; /* Visual cue it's interactive */
                    user-select: none;
                }
                .toggle-btn {
                    width: 20px;
                    text-align: center;
                    margin-right: 10px;
                    font-size: 1.2em;
                    line-height: 1;
                    color: #333;
                }

                /* Intro and Details Content */
                .intro-content {
                    padding: 10px 0;
                    border-bottom: 1px solid #eee;
                    margin-bottom: 10px;
                }

                .details-content {
                    padding: 10px 0 15px;
                    /* Start hidden */
                    display: none; 
                }

                /* State-dependent styles */
                :host([expanded]) .details-content {
                    display: block;
                }
                :host([expanded]) .header .toggle-btn::before {
                    content: '−'; /* Minus when expanded */
                }
                :host(:not([expanded])) .header .toggle-btn::before {
                    content: '+'; /* Plus when collapsed */
                }

                /* Expand More Button Styling (when collapsed) */
                .expand-more-btn {
                    padding: 8px 15px;
                    background-color: #007bff;
                    color: white;
                    border: none;
                    border-radius: 4px;
                    cursor: pointer;
                    margin-top: 10px;
                    transition: background-color 0.2s;
                }
                .expand-more-btn:hover {
                    background-color: #0056b3;
                }
            </style>
            <div class="details-container">
                <header class="header">
                    <span class="toggle-btn"></span>
                    <slot name="header"></slot>
                </header>

                <!-- Intro part (Always visible) -->
                <div class="intro-content">
                    <slot name="intro"></slot>
                </div>

                <!-- Details part (Conditionally visible) -->
                <div class="details-content">
                    <slot name="details"></slot>
                </div>

                <!-- Expand More Button (Visible only when collapsed) -->
                <button class="expand-more-btn" id="expand-more-btn">Expand more</button>
            </div>
        `;

        // Re-reference the elements after injection
        this.header = this.shadowRoot.querySelector('.header');
        this.expandMoreBtn = this.shadowRoot.getElementById('expand-more-btn');
    }

    connectedCallback() {
        // Initialize state based on whether the component should be expanded initially
        if (this.hasAttribute('expanded')) {
            this.isExpanded = true;
            this.setAttribute('expanded', '');
        }
        // Set up the initial toggle listener on the header
        this.header.addEventListener('click', this.toggle.bind(this));

        // Set up the expand more button listener
        this.expandMoreBtn.addEventListener('click', this.toggle.bind(this));
    }

    disconnectedCallback() {
        // Clean up listeners to prevent memory leaks
        this.header.removeEventListener('click', this.toggle.bind(this));
        this.expandMoreBtn.removeEventListener('click', this.toggle.bind(this));
    }

    // Toggles the expanded state
    toggle() {
        this.isExpanded = !this.isExpanded;

        // Update the attribute used by CSS for styling
        if (this.isExpanded) {
            this.setAttribute('expanded', '');
        } else {
            this.removeAttribute('expanded');
        }
    }
}

// Define the custom element
customElements.define('x-details', XDetails);
```

### How to Use It (Example HTML)

You can use this component by linking the JavaScript file:

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <title>X-Details Component</title>
    <script src="x-details.js" defer></script>
</head>
<body>

    <h1>Custom Details Component Example</h1>

    <!-- Example 1: Collapsed by default -->
    <x-details>
      <span slot="header">Recipe Instructions</span>
      <div slot="intro">
        Mix the ingredients (flour, sugar, eggs) and preheat your oven to 350°F.
      </div>
      <div slot="details">
        Bake for 30 minutes until golden brown. Let it cool completely before serving. Enjoy!
      </div>
    </x-details>

    <!-- Example 2: Expanded by default (using the 'expanded' attribute) -->
    <x-details expanded>
      <span slot="header">About Web Components</span>
      <div slot="intro">
        Web Components allow developers to create reusable, encapsulated UI elements.
      </div>
      <div slot="details">
        The Shadow DOM provides style and structure isolation, ensuring your component looks the same everywhere, regardless of external CSS.
      </div>
    </x-details>

</body>
</html>
```

### Explanation of Features

1.  **Shadow DOM:** Used to encapsulate all CSS and structure, preventing external styles from leaking in and preventing the component from polluting the global CSS namespace.
2.  **Slots:** The `slot="header"`, `slot="intro"`, and `slot="details"` allow the user to inject content while the component controls the layout.
3.  **Collapsed View:** When `isExpanded` is `false`, the `slot="intro"` is visible, and the `expand-more-btn` is visible, fulfilling the requirement. The `slot="details"` is hidden by CSS (`display: none`).
4.  **Styling:** The header is styled with a bottom border and a larger font. The `toggle-btn` uses `::before` content (`+` or `−`) to dynamically change the icon based on the component's state (checked via the `:host([expanded])` selector).
5.  **Functionality:** Both clicking the **header** and clicking the **"Expand more" button** trigger the same `toggle()` function, ensuring consistent behavior.
6.  **State Management:** The state (`isExpanded`) is managed by setting/removing the `expanded` attribute on the host element, which is a standard and clean way to influence component appearance via CSS.

